  "notes": "USAGE:\n{詫|わ}びる is more formal and literary than ⟦{謝|あやま}る→謝る：01177_ayamaru⟧ (to apologize). It implies deep, sincere remorse and is often used in written language, formal speeches, and news reports. The related noun {詫|わ}び means an apology, as in {詫|わ}び⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{入|い}れる→入れる：01098_ireru⟧ (to offer an apology). Not to be confused with ⟦{侘|わ}び→侘び：10655_wabi⟧ (the aesthetic concept of rustic simplicity), which is a different word.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {非礼|ひれい}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{詫|わ}びる: to apologize for rudeness\n- ⟦{深|ふか}く→深い：01211_fukai⟧{詫|わ}びる: to deeply apologize\n- {詫|わ}び⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{言葉|ことば}→言葉：02880_kotoba⟧: words of apology\n- {詫|わ}び⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{入|い}れる→入れる：01098_ireru⟧: to offer an apology",
